      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 3.9,
          "en": "We're now successfully fetching data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.9,
          "end": 7.053,
          "en": "but this data fetching code can be improved now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.98,
          "end": 11.97,
          "en": "For one, using all those then blocks here works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.97,
          "end": 14.43,
          "en": "and is definitely readable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.43,
          "end": 17.88,
          "en": "but many people prefer the async await syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.88,
          "end": 22.143,
          "en": "I briefly mentioned before, and you can use it here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.04,
          "end": 26.67,
          "en": "Now, what you should not do when using useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.67,
          "end": 29.64,
          "en": "is add the async keyword here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.64,
          "end": 32.22,
          "en": "and then try to use await here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.22,
          "end": 35.34,
          "en": "As you see, I'm already getting a warning in this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.34,
          "end": 37.68,
          "en": "that this is in the end not allowed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.68,
          "end": 39.753,
          "en": "or not supported by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.89,
          "end": 44.07,
          "en": "Instead, what you can do to use async await",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.07,
          "end": 46.53,
          "en": "inside of such a effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.53,
          "end": 49.02,
          "en": "is you can create a new function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.02,
          "end": 51,
          "en": "Because, of course, in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51,
          "end": 54.72,
          "en": "you can create functions inside of functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.72,
          "end": 56.763,
          "en": "which could be called fetchPlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.92,
          "end": 61.29,
          "en": "And here you can add async",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.29,
          "end": 64.77,
          "en": "because this is now simply a function defined by you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.77,
          "end": 67.05,
          "en": "not a function that would be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.05,
          "end": 69.273,
          "en": "in any special way by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.22,
          "end": 76.22,
          "en": "Now you can grab this code where you send the fetch request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.59,
          "end": 79.47,
          "en": "and await this, and as a result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.47,
          "end": 81.213,
          "en": "you'll get back the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.47,
          "end": 84.51,
          "en": "Then as a next step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.51,
          "end": 88.98,
          "en": "you can get the response data by awaiting response.json.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.596,
          "end": 95.46000000000001,
          "en": "And then as a last step, you can set the places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.46000000000001,
          "end": 98.973,
          "en": "as we did it before and now get rid of all that code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.05,
          "end": 101.34,
          "en": "And this code is, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.34,
          "end": 103.713,
          "en": "now a bit more readable and structured.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.94,
          "end": 107.37,
          "en": "Now, of course, now you also must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.37,
          "end": 110.58,
          "en": "that fetchPlaces gets executed though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.58,
          "end": 112.83,
          "en": "because at the moment, that's not happening,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.83,
          "end": 116.72999999999999,
          "en": "and therefore here still in the effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.72999999999999,
          "end": 118.97999999999999,
          "en": "But outside of fetchPlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.97999999999999,
          "end": 121.473,
          "en": "you should call fetchPlaces like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.67,
          "end": 125.97,
          "en": "So you define it and then you immediately call it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.97,
          "end": 129.33,
          "en": "But by defining it and decorating it with async,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.33,
          "end": 131.253,
          "en": "you can use this await keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.15,
          "end": 135,
          "en": "So that's a nice little and pretty common trick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135,
          "end": 138.57,
          "en": "for using async await in an effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.57,
          "end": 140.7,
          "en": "And with that, if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
